.TH cc 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
cc \- the C compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cc
[\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-S\fR|\fB\-E\fR] [\fB\-o\fI out\fR] [\fB\-O\fIn\fR] [\fB\-D\fIname\fR[\fB=\fIvalue\fR]] [\fB\-I\fIdir\fR] [\fB\-L\fIdir\fR] [\fB\-l\fIlib\fR] [\fB\-M\fR] [\fB\-X\fR] \fIfile\fR ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cc
compiles C on the machine itself.  From
.B prog.c
it produces
.BR prog.bc ,
which is a program in its own right:
.BR ./prog.bc .
.PP
Given a
.B .bas
file it runs
.BR mmbc (1)
first and compiles the C that comes out, so a BASIC program can be built
in one step.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " out"
Name the output.  May be given only once.
.TP
.B \-c
Compile to an object file and stop.
.TP
.B \-S
Stop after code generation.
.TP
.B \-E
Run the preprocessor only, and write to standard output.  One input file
only.
.TP
.BI \-O n
Optimisation level, 0 to 3.
.TP
.BI \-D name
.TP
.BI \-D name = value
Define a macro.
.TP
.BI \-I dir
Another directory to look in for headers.
.TP
.BI \-L dir
Another directory to look in for libraries.
.TP
.BI \-l lib
Link against a library.
.TP
.B \-M
Write a map file.
.TP
.B \-X
Keep the temporary files.
.SH WHAT IT PRODUCES
Bytecode with spans of native ARM Thumb in it, run by
.BR bcrun (1).
Headers live in
.BR /usr/lib/cc/include ,
and describe what
.B bcrun
provides rather than what the FUZIX libc does.  The library is resolved
by name at load time.
.SH LIMITS WORTH KNOWING
The compiler is small.  Deeply nested expressions and very large
functions can exceed it.
.PP
It also has a threshold past which a function stops being turned into
native ARM and falls back to bytecode, which is worth two to three times
on a hot loop.  If a small change makes a program suddenly slower, that
is the first thing to suspect;
.B BCRUN_BYTECODE=1
forces bytecode everywhere so the two can be compared.
.PP
The preprocessor is the board's own, not
.BR "gcc \-E" .
Expect C89 with some of C99: 160 of 175 conformance tests pass here.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# cc hello.c
# ./hello.bc
# cc -o prog.bc prog.c
# cc -E prog.c
# cc prog.bas
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bcrun (1),
.BR bcdump (1),
.BR mmbc (1),
.BR cpp (1)
